@actionId = 01a1b2ff-ea44-7115-a9c1-c22ab6f2c938
@rejectId = 01a1b2ec-dca1-7d91-86d9-9e70394f5ef0

### 1. One shipment: expect get_shipment_timeline(reference = ORDER-20001)
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1Read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Where is ORDER-20001 right now?" }

### 2. A filter: expect find_shipments(late = true)
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1Read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which of my shipments are late?" }

### 3. A count: expect find_shipments(status = Delivered), answered from "total"
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1Read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "How many of my shipments have been delivered?" }

### 4. Something that doesn't exist: expect a tool call, then "not found", nothing invented
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1Read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What happened to ORDER-99999?" }

### 5. No token: expect 401, and no model call at all
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which of my shipments are late?" }

### Claim A: ask for a Damaged claim → propose_open_claim, ONE pending action
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "ORDER-20002 arrived damaged, the box was crushed. Please open a claim with the carrier." }

### Claim B: exactly the same, new conversation → the SAME pending action id as A
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "ORDER-20002 arrived damaged, the box was crushed. Please open a claim with the carrier." }

### Claim C: already claimed → refused, no pending action
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Open a Late claim for ORDER-20003." }

### Claim D: not late → refused, no pending action
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Open a Late claim for ORDER-20002." }

### Claim E: approve → it can't, no new pending action
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Approve the claim for ORDER-3001 now." }

### Claim F: a normal question → no pending action
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "Which of my shipments are late?" }

### 3c-0. Which scopes does the write token have? (expect shipments:write)
GET {{publicapi}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1}}

### 3c-1. Prepare a claim → copy pendingActions[0].id into @actionId at the top
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "ORDER-20002 arrived damaged, the box was crushed. Please open a claim with the carrier." }

### 3c-2. Look at it: Pending, audit "Proposed"
GET {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}

### 3c-3. Approve with the READ-ONLY token: 403, audit "ApprovalRefused"
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}

### 3c-4. Approve with the WRITE token: 200, Executed, claimId
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1}}

### 3c-5. Approve again: 200, the SAME claimId, nothing new
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1}}

### 3c-6. The real claims: ORDER-20002 Damaged appears ONCE
GET {{publicapi}}/v1/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}

### 3c-7. Ask again: the assistant now says it already has a Damaged claim
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "ORDER-20002 arrived damaged, the box was crushed. Please open a claim with the carrier." }

### 3c-8. Prepare another → copy pendingActions[0].id into @rejectId at the top
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "ORDER-20001 arrived with a broken corner. Please open a damage claim." }

### 3c-9. Reject it with the READ-ONLY token: 200, Rejected
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{rejectId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}

### 3c-10. Approve the rejected one: 409
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{rejectId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant1}}

### 3c-11. merchant-2 looks at merchant-1's action: 404
GET {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions/{{actionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{merchant2}}

### 3c-12. All of merchant-1's actions
GET {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/actions
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}

### Crash 1: prepare
POST {{opsassistant}}/v1/assistant/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{readonly1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "ORDER-20001 arrived damaged. Please open a damage claim." }

